-	About 600 jobs have been maintained in at least 98 beneficiary MSMEs that avoided bankruptcy and closing, including 21 freelancers that have been involved in diverse Programme activities of MSME support (digital service providers and business consultants).
-	More than 1000 individuals from both banks have improved their entrepreneurial skills and knowledge through the periodic webinars, Conferences, roundtables, workshops, etc.
Temporary Jobs:
-	112 Jobs created during the reconstruction works on social infrastructure objects;
- 	12 jobs created as a result of implementation of small grants.
2.	23 new businesses have been created/strengthened due to implementation of the Start for Youth Plus support programme; (65% owned by women, 100% on left bank).
3.	16 new local communities (7 on right bank and 9 on left bank) benefitting from small infrastructure projects 
4.	Around 350 NGOs and Professionals are involved in development of their 5 Cross -River Thematic Sectoral platforms, supported by EU CBM 5 grants
5.	14 joint collaborative infrastructure projects implemented
6.	Due to COVID limitations, several cultural public events planned to be conducted in Bender fortress had to be rescheduled. Nevertheless, Youth Orchestra managed to conduct &#x201c;Rock Symphony&#x201d; Concert in Fortress in summer 2021 during short &#x201c;green code&#x201d; window. &#x201c;Legend of Moldova&#x201d; Folk Concert that was initially planned for Bender Fortress had to be conducted in Chisinau Green Theater. 8 Theater performances played by Chekhov theater in village Culture Houses renovated by CBM programme on both banks. All together &#x2013; 13 common cultural events since start of the programme. 
7.	Despite COVID limitations, over 3 900 individuals (approximately 50% men and 50% women) at 11 various common cultural events 
8.	12 (2 Flagship projects and 10 small scale) cultural infrastructure projects under various stages of implementation: 
&#x2022;	Bender Fortress-technical expertise and detailed design are completed; conservation works started;
&#x2022;	Chisinau Circus - technical expertise is completed; design in final stages, tender for restauration works is announced; Small scale projects &#x2013; 3 are completed; 7 will be realized in 2022;
9.	2 small cultural heritage projects finalized, for other 3 &#x2013; implementation period was extended to 2022.
10.	15 co-productions broadcasted/ 2 to be broadcasted in 2022. 
11.	9 media diffusions on prime time, 4 out of them in Transnistrian region</narrative>
